From 084245ecd52bd78591cfc89087f05b27df71a304 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:55:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] umi: CPU frequency scaling: an EPSS governor for the three
 clusters (sweet_cpufreq.c)

SM8250's EPSS cpufreq-hw: each domain's level table at 0x100, the request at
0x320. A thread every 16 ms reads each core's idle time (recount, through
machine_routines.c sweet_cpu_sample()) and picks the level its busiest core
needs (schedutil-like, x1.5 headroom, the top at 75% busy; up at once, down
after 64 ms). TSENS caps the gold and prime clusters over 75 C (sweetthermal).
A touch boosts every cluster to its cap for 250 ms (sweetboost). A stats line
every 10 s (sweetcpustats). sweetcpufreq=0: measure only; sweetcpugov=0: all at top.

Adapted from ios-apollo (xnu 0095, 0098, 0153, 0160; MIT, notice in the file).
First boot on the Mi 10: idle at 288 / 710 / 844 MHz, hottest core 57-60 C.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
